Of course, the *only* reason to play Nethack is for your own enjoyment. 
Each person should play as he likes. And I'm sure that I, too, learned 
aspects of playing style while trying to play the racket. So I have no 
objection to either of these two points.

What I object to is this advice being given to newbies as though it were 
the only worthwhile method of play. I also object to the extravagent 
claims made for the racket. Since most people agree that the early game 
is the most challenging part, one would assume that the early armor 
class boost would propel most protection-racket characters at least up 
to the ascension run. But that was not my experience while trying to 
play the racket. My experience was that even when I got my characters to 
the Minetown temple and donated for armor class, I would still 
frequently die trying to get back up to dlvl 1, due to losing my pet 
(either to the Watch Captain or simply too much fighting in general or a 
trap) and not having the hp to engage in combat, even with good AC.

I find that moderate pacifism in the early game works well for my weak 
starting characters. Yes, do let your pet buff up and do much of the 
fighting; do tame other tamable monsters; and perhaps attempt to get to 
Minetown at low XL (not necessarily level one) if the Mines are lit, I'm 
playing a lawful, dwarf, or gnome, and I have starting cash. (Usually, 
I'll head for Sokoban first, however.)

